# Guide-divider panel composition

Private parameter: `marker_panel=second|third`. The isolated guide marker selects
a four-neighbor region cut off by the main guide wall. The named source panel is
copied into that region and the other source panel into the remaining region;
on wall cells the named panel has foreground priority. `second` is the exact
public parent. Inputs are matched across settings.

A floods the marker-side region without crossing the guide wall. B consumes that
input-dependent mask to choose source pixels for the fourth panel. Generated
layouts include horizontal, vertical, diagonal and bent walls, row and 2x2 panel
arrangements, and a substantive 30x30 case.
